   "result": "I haven't entered this order, because amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, with little added blood pressure benefit. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify a higher dose.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO daily**, the typical starting dose. It can be titrated up to 10 mg after 1-2 weeks.\n- **Amlodipine 2.5 mg PO daily**, if the patient is frail or elderly or on other antihypertensives.\n\nIf the BP isn't controlled at 10 mg, the usual next step is to add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic, rather than escalate amlodipine.\n\nIf 20 mg is intentional, for example a specific specialist recommendation, tell me and I can note the rationale. It will likely trigger a pharmacy or CDS dose-range alert, and it may need attending co-signature or pharmacist verification under your hospital's policy.\n\nAlso, I don't see an order-entry tool in this session. Even once the dose is confirmed, you'd need to place the order in your EHR, though I can help you draft the order text.",
